(3995715, 566378, 52336, '<td valign="top">The blocky nature of it made by the dark walls, carpet, door pattern, but especially the heavy shadow on the near wall would have made this for me, but the kinetic little shadowy guy clambering around the only lit wall, casting irregularity over everthing with his blurriness and shadow, is really quite stirring.</td>', 'The blocky nature of it made by the dark walls, carpet, door pattern, but especially the heavy shadow on the near wall would have made this for me, but the kinetic little shadowy guy clambering around the only lit wall, casting irregularity over everthing with his blurriness and shadow, is really quite stirring.', '2007-08-14 00:29:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(3995735, 566097, 67373, '<td valign="top">I missed this image when I was voting for this challenge. Too bad - I was hoping to find a "10" image - and this one should have been it! Very nice work.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-08-13 23:35:29.</i></td>', 'I missed this image when I was voting for this challenge. Too bad - I was hoping to find a "10" image - and this one should have been it! Very nice work.', '2007-08-14 00:34:46.000000', '2007-08-14 00:35:29.000000', 0),
(3995893, 566876, 69008, '<td valign="top">I think that the shadow not being the most predominant element of this image got it the lower score, and also, voters seem to tend to give better scores to images that they find pleasant to view. This strikes a chord with me. Powerful image, with good thought going into the setup. I  like the way you brought the photo in the image into strong focus with the available light.  The "fuzz" works too, and adds to the "depressed" effect.</td>', 'I think that the shadow not being the most predominant element of this image got it the lower score, and also, voters seem to tend to give better scores to images that they find pleasant to view. This strikes a chord with me. Powerful image, with good thought going into the setup. I  like the way you brought the photo in the image into strong focus with the available light.  The "fuzz" works too, and adds to the "depressed" effect.', '2007-08-14 01:37:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(3995907, 566706, 66384, '<td valign="top">You have such a good eye for spotting simple artistic images. You do it over and over. I really admire that ability.</td>', 'You have such a good eye for spotting simple artistic images. You do it over and over. I really admire that ability.', '2007-08-14 01:43:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3995985, 566743, 53814, '<td valign="top">Angela,<br/> <br/>I think everyone wants their photos to be appreciated. But, is it enough to have a few great photographers compliment your work or better to have a hundred people with limited photography experience give you that coveteted high DPC vote. Both are rewarding - it is satifying to learn how to play the DPC game, and it is equally, if not more, rewarding to observe how your powers of observation and technical prowness progress as you continue your own personal photo journey.<br/> <br/>Did you realize your efforts have been appreciated in this thread:<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=624708&amp;page=13" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=624708&amp;page=13</a> <br/>Congratulations!<br/> <br/>btw... I would have scored this an 8 and the horse shadow a 5. I think you made the right choice.<br/></td>', 'Angela, I think everyone wants their photos to be appreciated. But, is it enough to have a few great photographers compliment your work or better to have a hundred people with limited photography experience give you that coveteted high DPC vote. Both are rewarding - it is satifying to learn how to play the DPC game, and it is equally, if not more, rewarding to observe how your powers of observation and technical prowness progress as you continue your own personal photo journey. Did you realize your efforts have been appreciated in this thread://www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&FORUM_THREAD_ID=624708&page=13 Congratulations! btw... I would have scored this an 8 and the horse shadow a 5. I think you made the right choice.', '2007-08-14 02:18:11.000000', NULL, 0),
